MISSING_BODY_RESOURCE_REF:
BUILDER OWNS THIS — code-layer fix, NOT a runner bug, NOT a flow-file bug.

The controller endpoint declares a body field that references another resource (e.g. teamId, projectId, taskId) but it does NOT carry an `@BodyResourceRefs([{ parentField: '<field>', resource: '<parent-POST-path>' }])` decorator. Without it, flows-generator falls back to a `${uniqString}` placeholder — a random string that the API rejects with a generic 404 ("Team not found", "Project not found"). The 404 cascades through every dependent chain flow.

FIX (builder, in the controller file named in the diagnostic):
```ts
import { BodyResourceRefs } from '../../../../common/decorators/body-resource-refs.decorator';

@Post()
@HttpCode(201)
@ResourceCaptures({ fromPath: 'id', resource: '<this-resource>', pathParam: 'id' })
@BodyResourceRefs([
  { parentField: '<the-Id-field>', resource: '/api/v1/<parent-resource>' },
])
@ApiOperation(...)
async create(...)
```

Reference pattern: see `apps/api/src/modules/team/application/controllers/team.controller.ts` invite-member endpoint, where both decorators coexist and chain flows pass.

DO NOT remove @ResourceCaptures to silence this — it serves a different purpose (capturing this resource's own id for downstream chains). Removing it breaks every flow that depends on this resource.

CHAIN_AUTH_UNRESOLVABLE:
BUILDER: chain:crud-roundtrip emitter detected role-gating on this endpoint but cannot find a matching role-grant on the parent's create endpoint. The chain would 403 at runtime.

DECLARATIVE FIX — add ONE decorator on each side:

  ON THIS ENDPOINT (already declared via @x-requires-parent-role):
```ts
@Post()
@ApiExtension('x-requires-parent-role', {
  parentField: '<fk-field>',
  minimumRole: 'OWNER',
  acceptableRoles: ['OWNER', 'ADMIN'],
})
```

  ON THE PARENT MODEL'S CREATE ENDPOINT:
```ts
@Post()
@ApiExtension('x-on-create-grant-role', {
  role: 'OWNER',
  toCaller: true,
})
```

This declares that the user creating a Team becomes OWNER of it, so the same user can subsequently create Projects requiring OWNER role. The generator threads the same auth-bootstrap token through both create steps.

If the parent does not auto-grant a role (e.g. role assigned via invitation), use @x-on-create-grant-role with `kind: 'invitation'` and `via: '/api/v1/<path>'` so the chain inserts the invitation step. Until both decorators exist, the chain flow is intentionally NOT emitted — better to surface this diagnostic than ship a 403-failing flow.
